256
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,840
Of course they're listening to you.

257
00:14:47,130 --> 00:14:48,510
Everybody listens to you.

258
00:14:49,130 --> 00:14:52,390
Monica, do you really think I should try this phasing-out thing?

259
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:54,180
I think you look fine.

260
00:14:58,180 --> 00:15:00,560
- Whenever you're ready.     - Okay.

261
00:15:01,730 --> 00:15:03,610
Hey, Timmy.

262
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:06,730
I've got a surprise...

263
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,440
for you.

264
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:10,280
Hold it. I'm sorry.

265
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:13,950
The surprise is a new swing set. If you could play it less intense.

266
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:18,160
Oh, yeah. Sure, no problem. Just hold on one second.

267
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,960
Hey, Timmy.

268
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:30,550
I've got a surprise for you.

269
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:31,720
Oh, my God!

270
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:41,770
So that's why I feed my dog Purina One.

271
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,600
Pick up a bag today.

272
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,320
- That's where you pick up the bag.     - Exactly.

273
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:53,280
No, the line is, "Pick up a bag," so you need to pick up the bag.

274
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:56,820
Or I could just point to it. Huh?

275
00:15:56,990 --> 00:16:01,960
Blah, blah, blah. Purina One. Point to a bag today.

276
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,460
- I didn't get it, did I?     - No.

277
00:16:07,630 --> 00:16:08,920
Yeah, okay.

278
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:13,510
Hi.

279
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,430
I'm Joey Tribbiani.

280
00:16:15,590 --> 00:16:18,220
I'm here to audition for "Man."

281
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,310
You mean "Dying Man."

282
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:22,810
Yes.

283
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:28,360
- Okay, come on. Do it one more time.     - Really? Really? Okay.

284
00:16:31,610 --> 00:16:33,440
Ross, this is Dr. McNeely...

285
00:16:33,610 --> 00:16:36,320
from Fake Accent University.

286
00:16:36,490 --> 00:16:38,830
We'd like you to come onboard with us full-time.

287
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:44,040
- Hey.     - Hey.

288
00:16:44,210 --> 00:16:45,620
Listen to this.

289
00:16:46,290 --> 00:16:48,500
My reading was wrong. I'm not going to die.

290
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:51,590
- Really? How do you know?     - Because my psychic is dead.

291
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:57,680
- She must have read the cards wrong.     - Oh, I'm sorry.

292
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:59,760
Ah, better her than me.

293
00:16:59,930 --> 00:17:02,060
Hey, let's bake cookies!

294
00:17:04,850 --> 00:17:06,180

295
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,770
Listen, I'm really glad you got the part.

296
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:14,190
- Are you sure you can do this?     - Yeah.

297
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,950
And, hey, thanks for coming with me.

298
00:17:16,110 --> 00:17:19,280
And thanks again for helping me take a shower.

299
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:25,200
Now, is that "never talking about it again"?

300
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:29,290
Hey, Joey. We're ready for you.

301
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,170
Joey, this is Alex. He's gonna be playing your son.

302
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:33,550
Hi, Alex.

303
00:17:33,710 --> 00:17:36,880
And, uh, as you can see, my hands are not in my pants.

304
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:40,300
Okay.

305
00:17:41,430 --> 00:17:44,680
All right, uh, Alex. Now, when Joey says his line:

306
00:17:44,850 --> 00:17:48,810
"Take good care of your mama, son," that's your cue to cry. Got it?

307
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:50,900
All right, let's do this.

308
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:56,740
Scene five, take one.

309
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,530
And action.

310
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:02,120
Take good care of your mama, son.

311
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,420
Take good care of your mama, son.

312
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:17,420
Come on, son.

313
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,220
Your mama's good people.

314
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:22,180
Cut.

315
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:25,180
Alex, remember, you're supposed to cry.

316
00:18:25,350 --> 00:18:27,600
- Can you cry for us this time?     - Okay.

317
00:18:27,770 --> 00:18:30,190
All right. From the top.

318
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,150
Scene five, take two.

319
00:18:35,650 --> 00:18:37,820
Take 36 is up.

320
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:40,200
Let's try this again.

321
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:41,700
You ready, Joe?

322
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:44,660
Uh, one thing, is it all right with you if I scream...

323
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:46,740
right up until you say, "Action"?

324
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:48,790
- Sure.     - Okay.

325
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:54,590
- Action!     - Take good care of your mama, son.

326
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:59,090
- Cut.     - Aah!

327
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:02,340
I'm sorry. Hey, hey. Joe, why don't you lift up your shirt?

328
00:19:02,510 --> 00:19:04,390
Take a look at this, kiddo.

329
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:11,350
We have a crying child! Roll the damn cameras!

330
00:19:16,690 --> 00:19:18,730
- Hello.     - Hello, is Ross there?

331
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,440
No, he's not. Can I take a message?

332
00:19:20,610 --> 00:19:23,030
Yes, this is Russell, Ross' divorce lawyer.

333
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,240
Just tell him that since I haven't heard from him...

334
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:27,660
I assume he's decided to give the marriage a try.

335
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:31,120
Ross got married again? Aah! No.

336
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:37,130
All right, keep going. We are phasing the accent out.

337
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:39,210
Phasing it out.

338
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:43,970
"So without retesting their results in the laboratory...

339
00:19:44,510 --> 00:19:47,680
the team would never have identified...

340
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:55,250
the initial errors in their carbon dating analysis."

341
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,480
Were there any questions at this point?

342
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:04,320
- Yes.     - What's happening to your accent?

343
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:10,120
Come again? What's this nonsense?

344
00:20:14,210 --> 00:20:16,960
All right. I'm not English.

345
00:20:18,590 --> 00:20:20,920
I'm from Long Island.

346
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:23,840
I was really nervous, and the accent...

347
00:20:24,010 --> 00:20:25,800
just, um... Just came out.

348
00:20:25,970 --> 00:20:28,180
Ha, ha. I'm sorry.

349
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:33,020
So if we could just get back to the lecture.

350
00:20:33,730 --> 00:20:36,980
Um, were there any questions?

351
00:20:39,690 --> 00:20:41,320
About paleontology?

352
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:47,700
All right, look, I was just trying to make a good first impression.

353
00:20:47,870 --> 00:20:49,740
Obviously, I screwed up.

354
00:20:49,910 --> 00:20:52,080
But what you guys think of me is really important...

355
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:55,290
because I'm hoping to get a permanent job here.

356
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:58,830
So if you'd just give me another chance to make a good impression...

357
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:02,510
Ross. Are you crazy?

358
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:06,050
I am still your wife? What, were you just never gonna tell me?

359
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,390
What the hell is wrong with you?

360
00:21:09,010 --> 00:21:10,970
Ugh, I could just kill you!

361
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:17,770
Well, hello, Rachel.

362
00:21:26,950 --> 00:21:29,660
- You've really done this before?     - Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

363
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:32,450
You just take a big, big swing, okay?

364
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,540
Now, don't hold back.

365
00:21:36,870 --> 00:21:39,000
- Hey.     - Hey.

366
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:40,380
What are you doing?

367
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:44,090
We're just celebrating that Joey got his health insurance back.

368
00:21:45,130 --> 00:21:46,800
Oh, all right.

